{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["And upon the nobles of the children of Israel He did not lay His hand — even though they saw the Elohim of Israel, the Holy One, blessed be He, did not lay His hand upon them. (Even though they saw the Elohim of Israel:) as written: כבלע את הקדש ומתו. And likewise regarding the men of Bet Shemesh: כי ראו בארון ה׳. And regarding Moshe Rabbenu: כי ירא מהביט. But here the Holy One, blessed be He, bestowed honor upon them, and on account of the cutting of the covenant He appeared to them, as I explained in the Covenant Between the Pieces, where it says: אשר עבר בין הגזרים האלה. And it is written there: ביום ההוא כרת ה׳ את אברם ברית וגו׳. And likewise further on, in the cutting of the covenant in the perashah Ki Tissa: וראית את אחורי. And it is written: ויעבור ה׳ על פניו וגו׳. And it is written after it: הנה אנכי כורת ברית." "And they ate and drank — they offered the burnt offerings and ate the shelamim, as it is written above: ויזבחו זבחים שלמים."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The parenthetical repetition of the phrase 'even though they saw the Elohim of Israel' appears to introduce the scriptural parallels that follow; rendered as found in the Hebrew text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:58.969227828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}